stateDiagram-v2
  %% Source: crates/shipyard-core/src/run.rs, Run::apply (the one transition table).
  [*] --> Queued
  Queued --> Claimed: Claim
  Claimed --> Planning: Start
  Planning --> PlanReview: PlanReady with human gate
  Planning --> Working: PlanReady without gate
  PlanReview --> Working: PlanApproved
  PlanReview --> Planning: PlanRejected
  Working --> SelfReview: BuildDone
  SelfReview --> Working: FixRound
  SelfReview --> PROpen: PrOpened
  PROpen --> ChangesRequested: ChangesRequested
  ChangesRequested --> Working: FixStarted
  PROpen --> Merged: PrMerged
  ChangesRequested --> Merged: PrMerged
  Working --> Merged: PrMerged in a fix round
  SelfReview --> Merged: PrMerged in a fix round
  Merged --> Done: Closed
  Working --> Done: Finished
  SelfReview --> Done: Finished

  state "Any active state (Queued to Merged)" as Active
  Active --> WaitingForAnswer: Ask
  Active --> Blocked: Block, an escalation (cause, last lines, stop report)
  Active --> RetryQueued: Retry
  Active --> Paused: BudgetStop or max turns
  Active --> Failed: Fail, runs of older logs only (Q-166)
  WaitingForAnswer --> Active: Answered, back to the return state
  WaitingForAnswer --> Blocked: Block, no answer after 72 h, keeps the return state
  RetryQueued --> Blocked: Block, breaker or retries spent, or guard failed for 30 min
  Blocked --> Active: Unblock or a reply on the ticket, one more round
  Blocked --> Done: Finished, a person closes a run with nothing to deliver
  RetryQueued --> Active: RetryDue
  Paused --> Active: Resume with budget left, more turns, or the next day for a day budget
  WaitingForAnswer --> Merged: PrMerged
  Blocked --> Merged: PrMerged
  RetryQueued --> Merged: PrMerged
  Paused --> Merged: PrMerged
  Active --> Cancelled: Cancel, kill switch, ticket terminal or pull request closed
  WaitingForAnswer --> Cancelled: Cancel
  Blocked --> Cancelled: Cancel
  RetryQueued --> Cancelled: Cancel
  Paused --> Cancelled: Cancel

  Done --> [*]
  Failed --> [*]
  Cancelled --> [*]

  note right of WaitingForAnswer
    A side state stores the return state.
    The stall timer and the budget clock run only in Planning, Working and SelfReview.
    Retry delay: min(10 s x 2^(n-1), 5 min).
    A failed guard waits with the same delay and uses no retry.
    Caps for the whole run: 3 failed attempts per step,
    4 review rounds, 3 feedback rounds, 8 fix rounds.
    The same failure twice in a row escalates at once.
  end note
